Source: foundry-emulators-computers
Section: metapackages
Priority: optional
Maintainer: Foundry Linux <packages@foundrylinux.org>
Build-Depends: debhelper-compat (= 13)
Standards-Version: 4.7.0
Homepage: https://foundrylinux.org/
Rules-Requires-Root: no

Package: foundry-emulators-computers
Architecture: all
Depends: ${misc:Depends},
 dosbox-x,
 hatari,
 fs-uae,
 mame,
 openmsx,
 openmsx-data,
 xemu
Description: vintage home-computer emulators (no bundled ROMs)
 Emulators that do not ship non-redistributable ROMs in the .deb.
 Suitable for inclusion in container images and ISOs without
 redistribution concerns:
 .
   * dosbox-x        DOS / x86 PC emulator (16-bit + early 32-bit)
   * hatari          Atari ST / STE / TT / Falcon
   * fs-uae          Amiga
   * mame            home computers with no dedicated emulator packaged —
                     notably the Camputers Lynx (drivers lynx48k, lynx96k,
                     lynx128k), plus Acorn, Amstrad, Apple II, Sinclair and
                     many others. Also listed in foundry-emulators-consoles
                     for its arcade/console coverage; apt de-duplicates, so
                     either metapackage alone brings it in
   * openmsx         MSX / MSX2 / MSX2+ / turboR
   * openmsx-data    OpenMSX system data files
   * xemu            Commodore 65/MEGA65/VIC-20/LCD, Enterprise, Primo, TVC
 .
 Note: MAME's "lynx" driver is the Atari Lynx handheld (atari/lynx.cpp),
 emulated here by mednafen in foundry-emulators-consoles. The Camputers
 Lynx home computer is the lynx48k/96k/128k drivers (camputers/camplynx.cpp).
 .
 Vintage emulators that ship non-redistributable ROMs in the .deb (VICE,
 Atari800, FBZX) live in foundry-emulators-vintage instead.
